The '''Deluge''' was a series of mid-17th-century military campaigns in the [[Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth]]. In a stricter sense, the term refers to the [[Swedish Empire|Swedish]] invasion and occupation of the Commonwealth as a theatre of the [[Northern War of 1655–1660]] only; in Poland and Lithuania this period is called the '''Swedish Deluge'''{{efn|({{langx|pl|potop szwedzki}}, {{langx|lt|švedų tvanas}}, {{langx|sv|svenska syndafloden}})}} or less commonly the '''Russo–Swedish Deluge''' ({{langx|pl|Potop szwedzko-rosyjski|link=no}})<ref>{{cite web|title=Potop szwedzko-rosyjski, czyli III wojna północna (Swedish–Russian Deluge, or the Third Northern War)|date=June 1, 2018|website=polskieradio.pl|url=https://www.polskieradio.pl/7/5102/Artykul/1980927,Potop-szwedzkorosyjski-czyli-III-wojna-polnocna|access-date=June 10, 2018|archive-date=January 6, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180106170338/https://www.polskieradio.pl/7/5102/Artykul/1980927,Potop-szwedzkorosyjski-czyli-III-wojna-polnocna|url-status=live}}</ref>{{better source needed|date=June 2019}} due to the simultaneous Russo-Polish War.<ref>{{cite book |last=Frost |first=Robert I |url=https://books.google.com/books?id=IfIbP8sfC0wC |title=After the Deluge. Poland-Lithuania and the Second Northern War, 1655–1660 |publisher=[[Cambridge University Press]] |year=2004 |isbn=9780521544023 |series=Cambridge Studies in Early Modern History |page=164}}</ref> In a wider sense, it applies to the period between the [[Khmelnytsky Uprising]] of 1648 and the [[Truce of Andrusovo]] in 1667, comprising the Polish theatres of the [[Russo-Polish War (1654–1667)|Russo-Polish]] and [[Second Northern War]]s.<ref>{{cite book |last=Subtelny |first=Orest |title=Ukraine. A history |publisher=Cambridge University Press |year=1988 |page=104 }}</ref> The term "deluge" (''potop'' in Polish) was popularized by [[Henryk Sienkiewicz]] in his novel ''[[The Deluge (novel)|The Deluge]]'' (1886).

During the wars, the Commonwealth lost approximately one third of its population as well as its status as a [[historical powers|great power]] due to invasions by Sweden and Russia.<ref>{{cite web|first=Marcin |last=Zawadzki |title=Durham University Polish Society |url=http://www.dur.ac.uk/polish.society/about_poland.htm |publisher=[[Durham University]] |access-date=June 23, 2009 |quote=During 'The Deluge', Commonwealth lost an estimated ⅓ of its population (proportionally higher losses than during World War II), and its status as a great power. |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20070821060613/http://www.dur.ac.uk/polish.society/about_poland.htm |archive-date=August 21, 2007 |url-status=dead }}</ref> According to [[Andrzej Rottermund]], manager of the [[Royal Castle, Warsaw|Royal Castle]] in [[Warsaw]], the destruction of Poland in the Deluge was more extensive than the destruction of the country in [[World War II]]. Rottermund claims that Swedish invaders robbed the Commonwealth of its most important riches, and most of the stolen items were never returned to Poland.<ref name="polskieradio.pl">{{Cite web|url=https://polskieradio.pl/art3_664603|title=Nikt tak nie ograbił Polski jak Szwedzi|website=PolskieRadio.pl}}</ref> Warsaw, the capital of the Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth, was destroyed by the Swedes, and out of a pre-war population of 20,000, only 2,000 remained in the city after the war.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.wilanow-palac.pl/pierwsze_zniszczenie_warszawy_i_jej_odbudowa_po_potopie_1655_1696.html|title=Pierwsze zniszczenie Warszawy i jej odbudowa po potopie 1655–1696|website=www.wilanow-palac.pl|access-date=December 25, 2021|archive-date=January 27, 2020|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200127192502/https://www.wilanow-palac.pl/pierwsze_zniszczenie_warszawy_i_jej_odbudowa_po_potopie_1655_1696.html|url-status=dead}}</ref> According to the 2012 Polish estimates, the material damage caused by the Swedish army amounted to 4 billion [[Polish złoty|złotys]]. 188 cities and towns, 186 villages, 136 churches, 89 palaces, and 81 castles were completely destroyed in Poland.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://dzieje.pl/aktualnosci/potop-szwedzki-przyniosl-polsce-straty-o-wartosci-4-mld-zlotych|title=Potop szwedzki przyniósł Polsce straty o wartości 4 mld złotych|website=dzieje.pl|access-date=December 25, 2021|archive-date=June 27, 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180627233246/http://dzieje.pl/aktualnosci/potop-szwedzki-przyniosl-polsce-straty-o-wartosci-4-mld-zlotych|url-status=live}}</ref>

