[[File:Venus von Willendorf 01.jpg|thumb|The [[Venus of Willendorf]], a figurine with exaggerated [[sexual characteristics]]. Estimated to have been made c. 30,000 years ago]]
'''Erotic art''' is a broad field of the [[visual arts]] that includes any [[Work of art|artistic work]] intended to evoke [[Sexual arousal|arousal]]. It usually depicts human [[nudity]] or [[sexual activity]], and has included works in various visual mediums, including drawings, engravings, films, video games, paintings, photographs, and sculptures. 

Some of the earliest known works of art include erotic themes, which have recurred with varying prominence in different societies throughout history.<ref>{{cite book |last1=Borg |first1=Sonia |title=The International Encyclopedia of Human Sexuality |chapter=Erotic art |date=2015 |pages=349–351 |doi=10.1002/9781118896877.wbiehs132|isbn=978-1-4051-9006-0 }}</ref> However, it has also been widely considered taboo, with either social norms or laws restricting its creation, distribution, and possession. This is particularly the case when it is deemed [[Pornography|pornographic]], [[Immorality|immoral]], or [[Obscenity|obscene]].

